{"name":"Tiger Moth","hex":"#f8f2dd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tiger moth","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Certain stout-bodied moths of the subfamily Arctiinae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiger_moth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arctiinae","blocks":[{"text":"The Arctiinae are a large and diverse subfamily of moths with around 11,000 species found all over the world, including 6,000 neotropical species. This subfamily includes the groups commonly known as tiger moths, which usually have bright colours, footmen, which are usually much drabber, lichen moths, and wasp moths. Many species have \"hairy\" caterpillars that are popularly known as woolly bears or woolly worms. The scientific name Arctiinae refers to this hairiness. Some species within the Arctiinae have the word \"tussock\"' in their common names because they have been misidentified as members of the Lymantriinae subfamily based on the characteristics of the larvae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Apantesis_phalerata.jpg/330px-Apantesis_phalerata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctiinae"},{"title":"Arctiini","blocks":[{"text":"The Arctiini are a tribe of tiger moths in the family Erebidae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Arctia_caja4.jpg/330px-Arctia_caja4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctiini"},{"title":"De Havilland Tiger Moth","blocks":[{"text":"The de Havilland DH.82 Tiger Moth is a 1930s British biplane designed by Geoffrey de Havilland and built by the de Havilland Aircraft Company. It was operated by the Royal Air Force (RAF) and other operators as a primary trainer aircraft. In addition to the type's principal use for ab initio training, the Second World War had RAF Tiger Moths operating in other capacities, including maritime surveillance and defensive anti-invasion preparations; some aircraft were outfitted to function as armed light bombers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/DH_82A_Tiger_Moth_-_N81DH.jpg/330px-DH_82A_Tiger_Moth_-_N81DH.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_Havilland_Tiger_Moth"},{"title":"Tiger","blocks":[{"text":"The tiger is a large cat and a member of the genus Panthera native to Asia. It has a powerful, muscular body with a large head and paws, a long tail and orange fur that fades to white in parts, with black, mostly vertical stripes. It is traditionally classified into nine subspecies, though some recognise only two subspecies, the mainland Asian tiger and the Sunda Islands tiger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Bengal_tiger_%28Panthera_tigris_tigris%29_female_3_crop.jpg/330px-Bengal_tiger_%28Panthera_tigris_tigris%29_female_3_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Woolly-Bear-Caterpillar.jpg/500px-Woolly-Bear-Caterpillar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Woolly-Bear-Caterpillar.jpg/500px-Woolly-Bear-Caterpillar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Banded woolly bear, Pyrrharctia isabella","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWoolly-Bear-Caterpillar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Copulation_in_tiger_moth.jpg/500px-Copulation_in_tiger_moth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Copulation_in_tiger_moth.jpg/1280px-Copulation_in_tiger_moth.jpg?utm_